  "scope": "Actual SDK guard/result types retained in a unit-return adapter. Codegen success alone is not a semantic or frame proof. Unit slot ABI, native source bridge installation, actual source/runtime/heap/child/oracle/TX2 and enclosing SDK caller remain required. Full10MiB domain applies only to explicitly marked full-bound candidates;58295 and1-byte cases are qualified restricted/diagnostic probes and cannot discharge that domain.",
  "review": "MaybeUninit contracts were stopped after large formula growth, even for one-byte backing: payload size is not the main cause. v3 was a lifetime-in-const compile error; v4 bridge codegen passed. v5 switched to the actual initialized Result error slot but needed immutable postcondition matching, repaired in v6. v6 and v7 unit contracts were also review-stopped. The conditional v7 bridge FAILED2/830 checks: shared BorrowRef Drop subtraction overflow and data-counter restoration;2/3 covers. A selected-property trace reproduces restoration failure. Its contract is not established, and the failed bridge is not a shipped-source counterexample. All stopped/failed/codegen cases are excluded from semantic acceptance."
}
